---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="What is a Physician Life Care Plan? — MyLifeCarePlanning.com"
  description="A physician life care plan is a comprehensive medical document prepared by a board-certified MD or DO that outlines the lifetime care needs and costs for an injured or disabled person."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="bg-brand-900 text-white">
      <div class="page-container py-12">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">What is a Physician Life Care Plan?</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-brand-200 max-w-2xl">A comprehensive medical document prepared by a board-certified MD or DO for injury and disability cases.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="page-container section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray">
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A physician life care plan is a detailed, evidence-based document prepared by a medical doctor (MD or DO) who holds specialized training in life care planning. It outlines every medical treatment, therapy, equipment, and care need an injured or disabled person will require over their lifetime — along with projected costs.</p>

        <h2>How is it different from a standard life care plan?</h2>
        <p>A standard life care plan can be prepared by nurses, rehabilitation counselors, or occupational therapists. A physician life care plan is authored by a medical doctor who has independent clinical authority to diagnose conditions, interpret imaging, and formulate treatment recommendations without requiring sign-off from a treating physician.</p>
        <p>This distinction matters significantly in litigation. A physician who prepares the plan can defend every recommendation from a clinical standpoint during deposition and trial cross-examination.</p>

        <h2>Who uses physician life care plans?</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Personal injury attorneys</strong> who need a credible expert to withstand Daubert challenges</li>
          <li><strong>Insurance carriers</strong> evaluating large catastrophic injury settlements</li>
          <li><strong>Defense counsel</strong> who need an independent medical evaluation of plaintiff claims</li>
          <li><strong>Courts and mediators</strong> seeking objective future care cost projections</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What does a physician life care plan include?</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Medical history review and clinical assessment</li>
          <li>Future surgical procedures and medical treatments</li>
          <li>Rehabilitation and therapy requirements</li>
          <li>Durable medical equipment and adaptive technology</li>
          <li>Home health care and attendant care needs</li>
          <li>Medications and pharmaceutical costs</li>
          <li>Transportation and accessibility modifications</li>
          <li>Psychological and psychiatric care</li>
          <li>Cost projections with replacement schedules</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="not-prose mt-10 p-6 bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-xl text-center">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-900 mb-2">Find a Physician Life Care Planner</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Browse our directory of board-certified MDs and DOs by state.</p>
          <a href="/physician-life-care-planners" class="btn-primary text-sm">Browse by State</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
